.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_CTX_SET_KEYLOG_CALLBACK 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_CTX_set_keylog_callback ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_get_keylog_callback ,
.Nm SSL_CTX_keylog_cb_func
.Nd logging TLS key material
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft typedef void
.Fo 
.Fa *SSL_CTX_keylog_cb_func
.Fc
(const SSL *ssl, const char *line);
.Ft void
.Fo SSL_CTX_set_keylog_callback
.Fa "SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "SSL_CTX_keylog_cb_func cb"
.Fc
.Ft SSL_CTX_keylog_cb_func
.Fo SSL_CTX_get_keylog_callback
.Fa "const SSL_CTX *ctx"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_set_keylog_callback
sets the TLS key logging callback.
This callback is called whenever TLS key material is generated or
received, in order to allow applications to store this keying material
for debugging purposes.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_keylog_callback
retrieves the previously set TLS key logging callback.
If no callback has been set, this will return NULL. When there is no key
logging callback, or if SSL_CTX_set_keylog_callback is called with NULL
as the value of cb, no logging of key material will be done.
.Pp
The key logging callback is called with two items: the
.Sy ssl
object associated with the connection, and
.Sy line ,
a string containing the key material in the format used by NSS for its
.Sy SSLKEYLOGFILE
debugging output.
To recreate that file, the key logging callback should log
.Sy line ,
followed by a newline.
.Sy line
will always be a NUL-terminated string.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn SSL_CTX_get_keylog_callback
returns a pointer to
.Vt SSL_CTX_keylog_cb_func
or NULL if the callback is not set.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssl 7
